@startuml
title MusicHub - Authorization Code Grant with PKCE S256

actor "Resource owner\nalumno.demo" as Owner
participant "Public web client\nmusic-web" as Client
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Authorization server\n/oauth" as Auth
participant "Resource server\n/api" as Resource
database "MusicHub database" as DB

Client -> Client: Generate code_verifier\nand state
Client -> Client: code_challenge = BASE64URL(SHA-256(code_verifier))
Client -> Browser: Redirect to /oauth/authorize\nresponse_type=code, client_id,\nredirect_uri, scope, state,\ncode_challenge, method=S256
Browser -> Auth: GET /oauth/authorize
Auth -> DB: Validate client, redirect_uri and scopes
DB --> Auth: Registered public client
Auth --> Browser: Login and consent page

Owner -> Browser: Enters credentials and approves scopes
Browser -> Auth: POST /oauth/authorize\nusername, password, approve=yes
Auth -> DB: Validate user password hash
Auth -> Auth: Create high-entropy code\nbound to user, client, redirect_uri,\nscope and code_challenge
Auth --> Browser: 302 redirect_uri?code=...&state=...
Browser --> Client: Callback with code and state
Client -> Client: Compare returned state\nwith original state

Client -> Auth: POST /oauth/token\ngrant_type=authorization_code\ncode, client_id, redirect_uri,\ncode_verifier
Auth -> DB: Load authorization code
Auth -> Auth: Validate one-use code,\nexpiration, redirect_uri and PKCE S256
Auth -> DB: Mark code as consumed
Auth --> Client: 200 access_token

Client -> Resource: GET /api/playlists\nAuthorization: Bearer access_token
Resource -> Resource: Verify JWT and playlists.read
Resource --> Client: 200 playlists

note over Client,Auth
The access token is returned only from /oauth/token.
It is never placed in the redirect URL.
end note
@enduml
